{"qid":"Q17167","names":["Roman Republic"],"title":"Roman Republic","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Roman Republic was the era of ancient Roman civilization from the overthrow of the monarchy around 509 BCE until the establishment of the Empire under Augustus in 27 BCE. Governed by elected magistrates, the Senate, and popular assemblies, it expanded from a city-state to dominate the Mediterranean. Internal strife and civil wars in the 1st century BCE led to its transformation into the Roman Empire.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. This polity has not yet received individual source review: treat extents as indicative atlas convention.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":"place/Roman-Republic","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Roman Republic","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Lucius Junius Brutus (cos.)","nativeName":"L. Iunius Brutus","roman":"L. Iunius Brutus","start":-509,"end":-509,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Lucius Tarquinius Collatinus (cos.)","nativeName":"L. Tarquinius Collatinus","roman":"L. Tarquinius Collatinus","start":-509,"end":-509,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Publius Valerius Publicola (cos.)","nativeName":"P. Valerius Publicola","roman":"P. Valerius Publicola","start":-508,"end":-504,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Titus Larcius Flavus (dict.)","nativeName":"T. Larcius Flavus","roman":"T. Larcius Flavus","start":-501,"end":-501,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Lucius Quinctius Cincinnatus (dict.)","nativeName":"L. Quinctius Cincinnatus","ro